WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.831
Harbor & Pine runs two cafés, Downtown and Riverside, with an owner, two shift leads, and a small crew. Let’s follow one day, and see how Worklynq keeps it running.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:20.753
Before the doors open, Maya, the owner, has the daily brief in her inbox: yesterday across both cafés, with sales, labour, and food safety.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:29.712
And what needs her first: the walk-in at Riverside ran warm last night, and Downtown needs avocados and oat milk before the next delivery.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:38.628
At Downtown, the team is already in. Each of them tapped Start my shift, or told Assist, and if you use Square, that clocks them in there too.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:46.960
Below, Operations has today’s work for each café: opening checklists, deliveries, temperature logs, and anything overdue.

00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:58.357
The lunch steam table is due a temperature check. Priya logs it from her phone: one hundred and forty-one degrees, inside the safe range. The inspector’s log fills itself.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:09.608
The dairy delivery arrives. In Inventory, one tap on Received, three cases of oat milk, and it’s in stock. What to order next is worked out from what sold in Square.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:19.680
Mid-morning, the dishwasher stops draining. Diego opens a maintenance request for Downtown, sets it to high priority, and names the repair company.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:24.443
It’s on the board with its own number, and Maya sees it at once, wherever she is.

00:01:25.233 --> 00:01:34.257
Around the counter, catering orders run through Order Tracking. The workshop lunch for twenty-five is in progress, and the muffins are now ready for pickup.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:41.185
A regular walks in for six almond croissants at two. It goes on the board as a walk-in, assigned to Sam.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:49.133
Over the counter, a TV shows every open order, and which ones are ready, so nobody has to ask.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:59.905
In the afternoon, Maya plans the weekend. Riverside is short on Saturday, so she adds a shift for Lena. Worklynq checks Lena’s food handler card is in date.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:09.297
At the end of the day, Completed shows what went out: orders, revenue, and the best sellers. Tomorrow morning, it all lands in the next daily brief.

00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:15.109
And whenever someone has a question, like what’s still waiting at Riverside, they just ask Assist.
